435,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.625,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":62.5,"pf":[],"description_full":"Annexon, Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, discovers and develops medicines for treating inflammatory-related diseases. The company provides Tanruprubart, an investigational full-length monoclonal antibody, which is in Phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of patients with guillain-barr\u00e9 syndrome; completed Phase II clinical trial for treating Huntington's disease; and in Phase 2a clinical trial for the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. It is also developing ANX007, an antigen-binding fragment (Fab) that is in Phase 3 program for the treatment of patients with geographic atrophy; and ANX1502, a novel oral small molecule inhibitor, which is in Phase 1 clinical trials for autoimmune indications. In addition, it develops ANX009, a C1q-blocking Fab that is in Phase I clinical trial for treating patients with lupus nephritis. The company was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Douglas E. Love Esq., J.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 97 people. Stock-based compensation of $169K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Annexon, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $748M market cap.","The company is burning through $186M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 3.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals a